WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.296
These are the attributes your team
already knows, and what each becomes.

2
00:00:04.296 --> 00:00:07.655
distinguishedName comes across,
but never use it for policy,

3
00:00:07.655 --> 00:00:09.876
because it's the placement we're leaving.

4
00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.475
Rules can't read manager or employeeType,

5
00:00:12.475 --> 00:00:15.225
which is why the program
keeps coded copies.

6
00:00:15.225 --> 00:00:20.216
The disabled bit becomes accountEnabled,
and every access rule should require it.

7
00:00:20.216 --> 00:00:24.870
And two have no attribute at all:
Kerberos service principal names stay

8
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:29.520
in AD until the workloads move, and
admin count gives way to roles and PIM.

9
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.130
So where do the values live?
